      director: `The value is the amount that must be in place before sex, the threshold before the act, and nothing else. In a scene look at two things. First, whether what the answer lists as required for this character (time known, a settled relationship, spoken love, privacy and safety, the pleasure expected) is in place now: when it is not, the step width is zero and the next move is building the missing condition (a high desire makes that tense). Second, when it is in place, the most ladder rungs one move may climb: 0-39 one rung, 40-69 up to two, 70-100 straight to the final move, and desire pushes within that (71 or more adds a rung; 91 or more goes straight to the final move when the scene allows it). The path is directness (straight in words, or through the body and the mood), the start is initiative, the place is publicOpenness. An established pair has a short and direct ladder. Drink, a romantic setting and the partner's availability lower the threshold for that turn only. Read it apart from the general spontaneity value, and never lower the threshold because openness is high. A missing value is not analyzed; do not assume one.`,
